# CLAUDE.md - Project Instructions for AI Agents

## Project Overview

This is a TouchDesigner project built on the Acro TD Core template.

## CRITICAL: Your TD Knowledge is Unreliable

TouchDesigner has a unique Python API. Your pre-trained knowledge about TD parameters, operator types, and API methods is often incorrect. ALWAYS:
- Call `td_guide` for reference documentation before starting any TD task
- Verify parameter names with `td_op` or `td_get_par` before setting them
- Use `td_children` to explore the scene before creating operators
- Use `td_find_empty` to check positions before creating new nodes

## MCP Tools

This project has MCP tools for interacting with the running TouchDesigner scene. Key tools:

| Tool | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `td_health` | Check if TD is running |
| `td_guide` | Get TD workflow guides (call before starting work) |
| `td_execute` | Run Python code in TD |
| `td_op` | Inspect operator parameters |
| `td_children` | List child operators |
| `td_get_par` / `td_set_par` | Read/write parameters |
| `td_layout` | See existing node positions |
| `td_find_empty` | Find clear spot for new nodes |
| `td_errors` | Check for errors/warnings |

## Key Paths

- `/` - Scene root
- `/AcroCore` - Main project component
- `/components/` - User components

## Conventions

- UpperCamelCase for public extension methods
- Extensions use sync-to-file (scripts/ directory)
- Custom parameters: Capitalized first letter (e.g., `Fadetime`)
- TD built-in params: lowercase (e.g., `tx`, `display`)
